# Frontend Quality Gates

Before any build or merge:

1. `npm run lint` — 0 errors, 0 warnings
2. `npm run typecheck` — no TypeScript errors
3. `npm run audit:check` — 0 vulnerabilities
4. `npm run deps:check` — dependencies match semver `wanted` versions
5. `npm run build` runs all checks automatically via `validate`

Never weaken ESLint rules to bypass warnings. Fix the code instead.

## After every change

Before marking work complete, run `npm run validate` in `markos-frontend` and fix all errors and warnings in **source files under `src/`**. Do not edit generated files under `.next/` — they are produced by Next.js and are excluded from lint via `eslint.config.mjs`.
